Let --enable-eventrecorder build without ImGui.

At scummvm master cd35134 the event recorder CALLS `isImGuiRecorderEnabled()`
unconditionally but only DECLARES it under `USE_IMGUI`, so configuring with
`--enable-eventrecorder` and no ImGui fails:

    gui/EventRecorder.cpp:432: error: 'isImGuiRecorderEnabled' was not declared in this scope
    gui/EventRecorder.cpp:862: error: no declaration matches
                                     'bool GUI::EventRecorder::isImGuiRecorderEnabled() const'

This is an upstream build break, not something specific to us -- ImGui is itself disabled
automatically when no enabled engine wants it, which is exactly the SCI-only case. Declare
the predicate always and define it as `false` when ImGui is absent.

FOR LOCAL DEBUGGING ONLY. If this is ever worth sending upstream it wants a proper look
rather than this stub.

APPLY WITH: (cd tools/scummvm-ref && git apply ../scummvm-patches/0002-*.patch)

diff --git a/gui/EventRecorder.cpp b/gui/EventRecorder.cpp
index f8ec2dd3..52379b88 100644
--- a/gui/EventRecorder.cpp
+++ b/gui/EventRecorder.cpp
@@ -859,6 +859,10 @@ void EventRecorder::deleteTemporarySave() {
 	_temporarySlot = -1;
 }
 
+#ifndef USE_IMGUI
+// LOCAL BUILD FIX -- no ImGui, so the ImGui recorder UI is simply never enabled.
+bool EventRecorder::isImGuiRecorderEnabled() const { return false; }
+#else
 bool EventRecorder::isImGuiRecorderEnabled() const {
 #ifdef USE_IMGUI
 	return debugChannelSet(-1, kDebugImGui);
@@ -866,6 +870,7 @@ bool EventRecorder::isImGuiRecorderEnabled() const {
 	return false;
 #endif
 }
+#endif
 
 #ifdef USE_IMGUI
 
diff --git a/gui/EventRecorder.h b/gui/EventRecorder.h
index c76738d3..ed2caa70 100644
--- a/gui/EventRecorder.h
+++ b/gui/EventRecorder.h
@@ -194,8 +194,11 @@ public:
 
 private:
 
-#ifdef USE_IMGUI
+	// LOCAL BUILD FIX: the recorder calls this unconditionally but only DECLARES it under
+	// USE_IMGUI, so `--enable-eventrecorder` without ImGui does not compile at this commit.
+	// Declared always; defined as `false` below when ImGui is absent.
 	bool isImGuiRecorderEnabled() const;
+#ifdef USE_IMGUI
 #endif
 
 	bool pollEvent(Common::Event &ev) override;
